            "topic_title": "About Threaditate"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_JThUHp": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is Threaditate?",
            "answer": "<p>Threaditate is a guided hands-on art kit that turns any photo into custom string art. You upload a photo, the app converts it into a step-by-step instruction sequence, and you follow along string by string until the piece is finished and ready to display. No crafting background needed. Everything ships in the box.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_JbjnLA": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Who is Threaditate for?",
            "answer": "<p>Threaditate was built for anyone who wants to make something by hand but doesn't want the overhead of figuring out a complicated craft. That includes first-time makers, experienced crafters looking for a more personal project, people who want a low-screen creative outlet, and anyone who's ever started a DIY kit and not finished it. If you have a photo that matters and a few hours to give it, Threaditate is for you.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_naaHUn": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What makes String Ring different from other string art kits?",
            "answer": "<p>Most string art kits give you a preset pattern and leave the rest to you. Threaditate gives you a guided session built from your own photo. The companion app converts any image into a real-time, step-confirmed instruction sequence, so you always know exactly where the next string goes. No other string art kit does this.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_VewiGw": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I restring my Threaditate?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes! Each Threaditate can be re-strung as many times as you’d like using the same frame. Simply remove the thread and start again with a new design.</p><p>If you’d like to create multiple pieces simultaneously, you’ll need additional kits, as each frame is designed to hold one artwork at a time.</p>"
          }
        }
